{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DCY8cqWURG5W1S8u3KEmd9","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"bca651cc37683143cadc43e8301cecf806b29738","date":"2026-10-07T23:09:52+03:00","message":"(test) Wait for the z-score tables before querying the height field (#837)","refs":"","body":"The first test in zscore-loading.test.tsx pays the cold dynamic import of the WHO\nreference tables. findByRole gives up after one second, and on the CI runner the\nimport sometimes takes longer than that, so the test fails with \"Unable to find\nrole=spinbutton\" while the form is still showing its loader. It failed that way on\nmain at 6a5b489 and on both CI runs of #834.\n\nThe test now awaits the promise loadZScoreReferences returned before looking for\nthe height field, so the one-second query timeout starts after the tables are\nloaded. The later tests in the file run against warm imports, which is why only\nthis one flakes. With the import delayed by 1.5 seconds locally, the test fails\nthe same way without this change and passes with it.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"6a5b489b47c58f526f9988624c0bf349ec5b75ad","date":"2026-10-07T14:56:38+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-6048: Accept numeric string height in calcWeightForHeightZscore (#832)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"solomonfortune","authorEmail":"solomonbuwule@gmail.com"},{"hash":"fcf1b2562d60389dbf88c5383c2d4237d9d1ff8a","date":"2026-10-05T15:02:05+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-6025: Load z-score tables only when a form needs them (#824)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Load z-score reference tables only for forms that use them\n\nThe WHO reference tables behind the z-score helpers are about 1.3 MB of JSON, and zscore-service imported all eight of them statically. The form engine app imports registerExpressionHelper from the library's entry at startup, so the tables ended up in its startup chunk, and every form open downloaded and parsed them whether or not the form used a z-score helper.\n\nEach table is a dynamic import now. useProcessorDependencies loads the tables for the z-score helpers a form's schema mentions, alongside the processor's own dependencies, so they're in place before initial values or any expression is evaluated. The helpers stay synchronous, because the expression evaluator doesn't await a helper's result before applying an operator to it. getZRefByGenderAndAge is split into one function per reference, so each helper only reads the tables it needs. If a table fails to load, the form still opens, the error is reported, and the helpers that need it return null.\n\nuseProcessorDependencies also reports loading from the first render. Once a form has opened, its field adapters and concepts are cached, so initial values could otherwise be computed before the dependencies had started loading.\n\nIn esm-form-engine-app the startup chunks go from 1,189 KiB to 382 KiB, or from 301 KiB to 114 KiB gzipped.\n\n* (fix) Wait for form dependencies before evaluating growth rules\n\n* Keep form state when the schema object changes\n\nResetting the form session whenever formJson was a new object wiped\nentered values in the patient chart. esm-form-engine-app passes a new\nschema object on every render, and it re-renders once the form is\nmarked dirty, so the first edit was lost.\n\nDrop the session reset in FormFactoryProvider and stop\nuseProcessorDependencies reloading on a new formJson object. The form\nbuilder already remounts FormEngine when its schema changes, so no\nconsumer relies on replacing a mounted schema.\n\n* fix: Wait for every subform before allowing submission\n\nTrack pending dependencies by form instance so a ready sibling cannot clear another subform’s loading state. Remove the instance from the pending set when it unmounts.\n\nCover pending and failed subform dependencies, retry, required-field validation and saving all subforms after recovery.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"c36156b258c75587af5c3051aa85feb41703b131","date":"2023-11-21T12:10:22+03:00","message":"(feat) Add Zscore functionality (#139)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) Add Zscore functionality\r\n\r\n* Remove unwanted expression function\r\n\r\n* Update the classes to functions\r\n\r\n* Update helper functions\r\n\r\n* Add tests to functions\r\n\r\n* address build errors\r\n\r\n* Address PR comments\r\n\r\n* Tests\r\n\r\n* Modify tests for zscore functions\r\n\r\n* Remove describe","authorName":"AJAL ODORA JONATHAN","authorEmail":"43242517+ODORA0@users.noreply.github.com"}],"totalCount":4}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b8e54bb-eabb-4d2f-ac3b-ec86ad229ea8","uuid":"24024ea2-1410-436e-8b5b-f53ff461c0cf","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:21:11.064Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"bca651cc37683143cadc43e8301cecf806b29738","date":"2026-10-07T23:09:52+03:00","message":"(test) Wait for the z-score tables before querying the height field (#837)","refs":"","body":"The first test in zscore-loading.test.tsx pays the cold dynamic import of the WHO\nreference tables. findByRole gives up after one second, and on the CI runner the\nimport sometimes takes longer than that, so the test fails with \"Unable to find\nrole=spinbutton\" while the form is still showing its loader. It failed that way on\nmain at 6a5b489 and on both CI runs of #834.\n\nThe test now awaits the promise loadZScoreReferences returned before looking for\nthe height field, so the one-second query timeout starts after the tables are\nloaded. The later tests in the file run against warm imports, which is why only\nthis one flakes. With the import delayed by 1.5 seconds locally, the test fails\nthe same way without this change and passes with it.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"6a5b489b47c58f526f9988624c0bf349ec5b75ad","date":"2026-10-07T14:56:38+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-6048: Accept numeric string height in calcWeightForHeightZscore (#832)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"solomonfortune","authorEmail":"solomonbuwule@gmail.com"},{"hash":"fcf1b2562d60389dbf88c5383c2d4237d9d1ff8a","date":"2026-10-05T15:02:05+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-6025: Load z-score tables only when a form needs them (#824)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Load z-score reference tables only for forms that use them\n\nThe WHO reference tables behind the z-score helpers are about 1.3 MB of JSON, and zscore-service imported all eight of them statically. The form engine app imports registerExpressionHelper from the library's entry at startup, so the tables ended up in its startup chunk, and every form open downloaded and parsed them whether or not the form used a z-score helper.\n\nEach table is a dynamic import now. useProcessorDependencies loads the tables for the z-score helpers a form's schema mentions, alongside the processor's own dependencies, so they're in place before initial values or any expression is evaluated. The helpers stay synchronous, because the expression evaluator doesn't await a helper's result before applying an operator to it. getZRefByGenderAndAge is split into one function per reference, so each helper only reads the tables it needs. If a table fails to load, the form still opens, the error is reported, and the helpers that need it return null.\n\nuseProcessorDependencies also reports loading from the first render. Once a form has opened, its field adapters and concepts are cached, so initial values could otherwise be computed before the dependencies had started loading.\n\nIn esm-form-engine-app the startup chunks go from 1,189 KiB to 382 KiB, or from 301 KiB to 114 KiB gzipped.\n\n* (fix) Wait for form dependencies before evaluating growth rules\n\n* Keep form state when the schema object changes\n\nResetting the form session whenever formJson was a new object wiped\nentered values in the patient chart. esm-form-engine-app passes a new\nschema object on every render, and it re-renders once the form is\nmarked dirty, so the first edit was lost.\n\nDrop the session reset in FormFactoryProvider and stop\nuseProcessorDependencies reloading on a new formJson object. The form\nbuilder already remounts FormEngine when its schema changes, so no\nconsumer relies on replacing a mounted schema.\n\n* fix: Wait for every subform before allowing submission\n\nTrack pending dependencies by form instance so a ready sibling cannot clear another subform’s loading state. Remove the instance from the pending set when it unmounts.\n\nCover pending and failed subform dependencies, retry, required-field validation and saving all subforms after recovery.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"c36156b258c75587af5c3051aa85feb41703b131","date":"2023-11-21T12:10:22+03:00","message":"(feat) Add Zscore functionality (#139)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) Add Zscore functionality\r\n\r\n* Remove unwanted expression function\r\n\r\n* Update the classes to functions\r\n\r\n* Update helper functions\r\n\r\n* Add tests to functions\r\n\r\n* address build errors\r\n\r\n* Address PR comments\r\n\r\n* Tests\r\n\r\n* Modify tests for zscore functions\r\n\r\n* Remove describe","authorName":"AJAL ODORA JONATHAN","authorEmail":"43242517+ODORA0@users.noreply.github.com"}],"totalCount":4}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DCY8cqWURG5W1S8u3KEmd9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
